INSERT INTO `features` (`id`, `module`, `feature_id`, `feature_desc`, `feature_desc_cn`) VALUES (39,3,1,'As a blog user, I want to access the Blog API application through its main function, so that I can interact with the blogging platform effectively. This core functionality enables users to initiate the application and perform various actions related to blog management. The main function serves as the entry point for users, ensuring that they can engage with the system\'s features seamlessly, thereby enhancing their overall experience with the blogging service.',NULL),(40,3,2,'As a blog user, I want to retrieve a list of blog posts by title and category ID so that I can easily find content relevant to my interests. The system provides this functionality through the BlogService, BlogServiceImpl, and BlogMapper classes, which work together to ensure that when I specify a title and category ID, the appropriate blog posts are fetched efficiently. This allows me to navigate the content effectively based on my preferences.',NULL),(41,3,3,'As a blog reader, I want to search for published blog posts using specific keywords, so that I can easily find relevant content that interests me. The system provides this functionality through the BlogController\'s searchBlog method, which interacts with the BlogService and BlogMapper to retrieve a list of published blogs based on my query. This ensures that I receive accurate and timely results tailored to my interests.',NULL),(42,3,4,'As a blog user, I want to retrieve a list of blog post IDs and titles so that I can easily browse and select posts of interest. The system provides this functionality through the BlogService, BlogServiceImpl, and BlogMapper classes, which collectively ensure that users can access relevant information efficiently. This streamlined process allows for quick identification of content without unnecessary complexity.',NULL),(43,3,5,'As a blog reader, I want to access a list of published blogs filtered by various criteria such as category name, tag name, and publication status, so that I can easily find relevant content. The system provides functionalities to retrieve new blogs, blog information lists by publication status, and archives based on year and month. By allowing filtering through categories and tags, the system enhances my ability to discover content that meets my interests.',NULL),(44,3,6,'As a blog administrator, I want to retrieve archived blog posts along with their published status counts, so that I can effectively manage and analyze the content available on the platform. The functionality provided by the methods \'getArchiveBlogAndCountByIsPublished\' in both \'BlogService\' and \'BlogServiceImpl\' allows me to access this information seamlessly, ensuring that I have a clear overview of which posts are published or unpublished, facilitating better content management.',NULL),(45,3,7,'As a blog reader, I want to receive a curated list of recommended and published blogs limited by a specific number, so that I can easily discover quality content that aligns with my interests. The system provides this functionality through the BlogService and its implementation in BlogServiceImpl, which retrieves random blog entries based on the specified criteria using the BlogMapper. This ensures that I have access to relevant and engaging blog posts tailored to my preferences.',NULL),(46,3,8,'As a blog administrator, I want to delete a blog and its associated tags by their respective IDs, so that I can manage content effectively and ensure that outdated or irrelevant posts are removed from the platform. The system provides functionality through methods like \'deleteBlogById\' and \'deleteBlogTagByBlogId\', allowing me to perform these actions seamlessly, ensuring that both the blog post and its related tags are deleted in a coordinated manner.',NULL),(47,3,9,'As a blog administrator, I want to save blog posts and associate them with relevant tags so that I can effectively manage content and improve discoverability for users. The system allows me to save a blog through multiple services, ensuring that the data is consistently stored across different layers of the application. Additionally, I can link tags to specific blogs using their IDs, enhancing the organization and categorization of posts within the platform.',NULL),(48,3,10,'As a blog administrator, I want to update the recommendation status and top priority of blog posts by their IDs, so that I can manage the visibility and importance of content effectively. This includes actions such as marking a blog as recommended or topping it through methods like updateBlogRecommendById and updateBlogTopById. Additionally, I want to update the entire blog post using the updateBlog function, ensuring that all necessary changes are made efficiently.',NULL),(49,3,11,'As a blog administrator, I want to update the visibility of a blog post by its ID, so that I can control who can see the content based on its current status. The system provides functionality through the BlogService and BlogServiceImpl classes to handle this action, ensuring that the visibility settings are accurately applied using the BlogMapper for database interactions. This allows me to manage blog content effectively and maintain appropriate access levels.',NULL),(50,3,12,'As a blog administrator, I want to update the view counts of blog posts in the system and synchronize this information with Redis, so that I can accurately track user engagement and ensure that the data is readily available for analytics. The system provides functionality through methods like updateViewsToRedis and updateViews, allowing me to input a blog ID and the number of views, ensuring that both the database and Redis cache are updated consistently.',NULL),(51,3,13,'As a blog reader, I want to retrieve blog details by ID, including its title and published status, so that I can access relevant content easily. Additionally, as an admin, I want to view blog statistics and the number of views for each post to understand engagement levels. This functionality is supported by methods like getBlogById, getTitleByBlogId, and getPublishedByBlogId across various service and controller classes.',NULL),(52,3,14,'As a blog administrator, I want to securely retrieve and verify the password for a specific blog using its ID, so that I can ensure proper access control and manage blog information effectively. The system provides functionality through methods like getBlogPassword in various services and controllers, allowing me to process and check blog passwords efficiently. This ensures that only authorized users can access sensitive blog data, enhancing security and user management.',NULL),(53,3,15,'As a blog administrator, I want to count the number of published blogs, categorize them by category ID, and tag them by tag ID so that I can analyze the distribution of content across different categories and tags. This will help me understand which topics are most popular and ensure that my blog remains relevant to readers. The system provides methods to count blogs based on their publication status, category, and tags, facilitating effective content management.',NULL),(54,3,16,'As a blog administrator, I want to check if comments are enabled for a specific blog post by using the blog ID, so that I can manage user interactions effectively. The system provides this functionality through multiple methods in the BlogService, BlogServiceImpl, and BlogMapper classes, which all retrieve the comment status based on the provided blog ID. This ensures that I can easily determine whether comments are allowed for each post.',NULL),(55,3,17,'As a blog administrator, I want to save and delete blog view data in Redis so that I can efficiently manage and optimize the performance of my blog\'s analytics. The \'saveBlogViewsToRedis\' function allows me to store the number of views for each blog post, while the \'deleteBlogRedisCache\' function enables me to clear outdated or unnecessary cache data, ensuring that the analytics reflect current user engagement accurately.',NULL),(56,3,18,'As a blog reader, I want to see the number of views for each blog post on the page so that I can gauge its popularity and relevance. The system retrieves view counts from Redis and updates the PageResult<BlogInfo> accordingly, ensuring that I have access to real-time data about blog engagement. This feature enhances my browsing experience by providing insights into which posts are most viewed, helping me make informed decisions about what to read.',NULL),(57,3,19,'As a blog user, I want to view a list of blogs by specifying the page number, so that I can easily navigate through the available content. Additionally, as a blog administrator, I want to manage and filter blogs by title and category while also controlling pagination through page size and page number parameters, so that I can efficiently organize and present relevant blog posts to users.',NULL),(58,3,20,'As a blog administrator, I want to delete blog posts by their ID so that I can manage and maintain the content on the platform effectively. This action allows me to remove outdated or irrelevant posts, ensuring that users have access to current and appropriate information. The ability to delete posts directly supports my goal of keeping the blog organized and relevant for its audience.',NULL),(59,3,21,'As an admin user, I want to manage categories and tags within the blog system so that I can organize content effectively and enhance user navigation. The \'categoryAndTag\' function allows me to categorize blog posts and assign relevant tags, ensuring that users can easily find related content. This functionality supports the core goal of improving content discoverability and organization, ultimately leading to a better user experience on the platform.',NULL),(60,3,22,'As an admin user, I want to update the \'top\' status of a blog post by providing its ID and a boolean value, so that I can manage which posts are highlighted or prioritized in the system. This functionality allows me to control the visibility and importance of specific blog content, ensuring that users see the most relevant information first.',NULL),(61,3,23,'As an admin user, I want to update the recommendation status of a blog post by providing its ID and a boolean value, so that I can manage which posts are recommended to users effectively. This functionality allows me to control the visibility and promotion of specific content, ensuring that users see the most relevant and high-quality posts based on my recommendations.',NULL),(62,3,24,'As a blog administrator, I want to update the visibility of blog posts using their unique ID and specified visibility settings, so that I can control which posts are accessible to users and maintain the desired level of content exposure.',NULL),(63,3,25,'As a blog administrator, I want to retrieve results based on the specified blog and type so that I can effectively manage and display relevant content. The getResult function allows me to access specific information related to the blog, ensuring that I can tailor the content according to user needs and preferences, thereby enhancing the overall user experience on the platform.',NULL),(64,3,26,'As a content manager, I want to retrieve the publication status and associated timeframes of blog posts by year and month, so that I can effectively analyze and manage the content based on its publication status. The function getGroupYearMonthByIsPublished allows me to access this information, enabling me to understand trends in published content over time and make informed decisions regarding future publications.',NULL),(65,4,27,'As a user, I want to view moments by navigating through pages and like specific moments, so that I can engage with content that resonates with me and express my appreciation for it. The \'moments\' function allows me to retrieve a list of moments based on the page number provided, while the \'like\' function enables me to show support for individual moments by liking them. Together, these actions enhance my interaction with the platform.',NULL),(66,5,28,'As a system administrator, I want the AccessLimitInterceptor to pre-handle requests so that I can enforce access limits effectively, ensuring that users do not exceed their allowed usage. This functionality allows the system to manage user access in real-time, providing immediate feedback on any violations and maintaining system integrity. By intercepting requests before they reach the handler, this feature supports proactive management of user permissions and enhances overall security.',NULL),(67,6,29,'As an administrator, I want to manage operation and exception logs by retrieving, saving, and deleting log entries so that I can effectively monitor system activities and troubleshoot issues. This includes accessing operation logs by date, saving new logs with relevant details such as username and IP address, and deleting specific logs when necessary. Additionally, I want to handle exceptions by logging errors with their descriptions to ensure comprehensive error tracking.',NULL),(68,7,30,'As a user, I want to send both simple and HTML template emails to specified accounts, so that I can effectively communicate with recipients using different email formats. Additionally, I want to retrieve my IP address and obtain city information based on it, ensuring that my location is accurately represented. Furthermore, I need utility functions to validate strings for emptiness and special characters, as well as to extract stack traces from exceptions for better debugging.',NULL),(69,8,31,'As a developer, I want to utilize hashing and serialization utilities to securely handle passwords and convert data structures, so that I can ensure data integrity and facilitate communication between different components of the application. The system provides methods for generating MD5 and MurmurHash32 hashes, verifying passwords with bcrypt, and converting objects to and from JSON format. These actions support secure password management and efficient data handling, addressing core needs for security and interoperability.',NULL),(70,9,32,'As a developer, I want to effectively manage request parameters and filter objects within the system so that I can ensure only relevant data is processed. The getRequestParams function retrieves the parameters from a given join point, while isFilterObject determines if an object should be filtered out. Additionally, isIgnoreParams checks if specific parameters should be ignored, allowing for streamlined handling of requests and improved performance in processing user inputs.',NULL),(71,10,33,'As a QQ user, I want to retrieve my QQ nickname and avatar URL based on my QQ number, so that I can easily identify myself and share my profile. Additionally, I want to upload images associated with my QQ account, ensuring they are stored correctly. The system provides functionalities to validate my QQ number and fetch the corresponding nickname and avatar URL, facilitating a seamless user experience in managing my online identity.',NULL),(72,11,34,'As a user, I want to manage my account by logging in with my username and password, checking my account status, and updating my information, so that I can ensure my account is secure and up-to-date. The system allows me to verify if my account is non-expired, non-locked, and enabled through various checks. Additionally, I can retrieve or update my user details using the provided methods for finding users by username or ID.',NULL),(73,12,35,'As a user, I want to securely log in and manage my login activity so that I can access the system safely and monitor my usage. This includes generating and validating tokens for authentication, logging my login attempts with details like status and IP address, and retrieving historical login logs by date. The system provides functionalities such as setting secret keys, handling successful or unsuccessful authentication attempts, and managing login logs through various services.',NULL),(74,13,36,'As a content creator, I want to convert markdown text to HTML and set specific attributes for HTML elements, so that I can ensure my content is displayed correctly and meets the required formatting standards. The system provides functionality to create markdown content, convert it to HTML through \'markdownToHtml\' and \'markdownToHtmlExtensions\', and allows me to customize the output by setting attributes using \'setAttributes\'. This streamlined process enhances my ability to produce well-structured web content.',NULL),(75,14,37,'As a content creator, I want to utilize the CoverExtension to create and extend various types of content nodes (HTML, text) so that I can effectively render and manage my markdown documents. This includes creating new nodes with specific contexts and extending existing parsers and renderers to support different node types. By leveraging methods like create() and extend(), I can ensure that my content is well-structured and visually appealing for my audience.',NULL),(76,15,38,'As a content creator, I want to create and extend Heimu extensions for rendering various types of content (HTML, text) so that I can effectively manage and display my markdown content. The system allows me to create instances of Heimu extensions and render nodes using specific contexts, such as HtmlNodeRendererContext and TextContentNodeRendererContext. Additionally, I can retrieve opening and closing delimiters, ensuring proper formatting in my documents.',NULL),(77,16,39,'As a blog administrator, I want to set the BlogService through the CommentUtils utility, so that I can manage and enhance the commenting functionality on my blog effectively. This action allows me to integrate specific services that support user interactions and content management, ensuring a seamless experience for users engaging with comments. By utilizing this method, I can ensure that the comment system is tailored to meet the needs of my blog\'s audience.',NULL),(78,16,40,'As a comment moderator, I want to manage notification settings and update comment statuses so that I can effectively oversee user interactions. The system allows me to set the notification channel for comments, determine whether notifications should be sent based on the type of comment (visitor or parent), and notify myself of relevant comments. Additionally, I can update the published status and notice flags for specific comments, ensuring that I maintain control over the visibility and management of user-generated content.',NULL),(79,16,41,'As a user managing comments, I want to be able to set default comment visibility, assign avatars, and send notifications related to comments so that I can enhance user engagement and streamline comment management. This includes actions like saving, updating, and hiding comments, as well as posting new comments with specific attributes. By having these functionalities grouped together, I can efficiently manage the comment system while ensuring that users receive timely updates and personalized experiences.',NULL),(80,16,42,'As a blog reader, I want to view comments by page and filter them by parent comment ID so that I can easily navigate discussions related to specific topics. The system provides functionality to retrieve lists of comments based on pagination and parent-child relationships through methods like getListByPageAndParentCommentId and getPageCommentList. Additionally, I want to access individual comments by their ID, ensuring I can engage with relevant content directly.',NULL),(81,16,43,'As a blog administrator, I want to manage and review comments on blog posts by retrieving comments based on pagination and blog ID, so that I can efficiently oversee user interactions and maintain the quality of discussions. Additionally, I want to view the count of comments for analytics purposes and access blog titles associated with specific IDs, ensuring that I have comprehensive oversight over comment activity.',NULL),(82,16,44,'As a user, I want to validate URLs to ensure they are properly formatted, so that I can confidently use them within the application without encountering errors or broken links. The isValidUrl function checks the validity of a given URL string, providing assurance that the URLs I input meet the required standards for functionality. This action supports my need for reliability and accuracy when sharing or utilizing web resources in my tasks.',NULL),(83,16,45,'As a blog administrator, I want to manage comments on my blog by updating their published status or notice and deleting comments by their ID or associated blog ID, so that I can maintain the quality of discussions and ensure relevant content is visible to readers.',NULL),(84,16,46,'As a blog administrator, I want to count the number of comments on a blog post by page and publication status, so that I can effectively manage and evaluate user engagement with my content. The system provides this functionality through the CommentService, CommentServiceImpl, and CommentMapper classes, which allow me to retrieve counts based on specific criteria such as pagination and whether comments are published or not.',NULL),(85,16,47,'As an admin user, I want to delete comments by their ID or directly through the comment object, so that I can manage and maintain the quality of content within the system. The functionality provided by both CommentServiceImpl and CommentAdminController allows for efficient removal of unwanted or inappropriate comments, ensuring a cleaner and more relevant user experience.',NULL),(86,17,48,'As a user, I want to upload images through various channels (GitHub, Local, File Upload) and manage notifications for these uploads so that I can efficiently share and store my images. The system provides functionality to set up notification channels, retrieve images by URL, and utilize different upload methods. This ensures I have flexibility in how I share my content while being notified of the status of my uploads.',NULL),(87,18,49,'As a Telegram user, I want to receive notifications about comments and manage them through commands, so that I can stay updated on interactions and respond effectively. The system allows me to notify myself of new comments, retrieve content related to those comments, and execute actions such as updating statuses or deleting comments via commands. This integration ensures seamless communication and management of my Telegram interactions.',NULL),(88,19,50,'As a system administrator, I want to manage scheduled jobs by creating, updating, deleting, and retrieving job details so that I can efficiently control job execution and monitor their statuses. This includes actions like saving job logs, running jobs by ID, and updating job statuses. The system provides methods for obtaining trigger keys and job keys, allowing me to interact with the scheduling framework effectively while ensuring that all operations are logged for accountability.',NULL),(89,20,51,'As a developer, I want to manage application context and retrieve beans from the Spring framework using methods like setApplicationContext, getBean, containsBean, and isSingleton, so that I can efficiently configure and utilize application components. This allows me to check for bean existence, determine their types, and ensure singleton behavior where necessary. Additionally, I want to create REST templates through restTemplate and restTemplateByProxy for seamless communication with external services.',NULL),(90,21,52,'As a site administrator, I want to manage site settings including adding, updating, and deleting configurations such as web title suffix and friend info content, so that I can ensure the website reflects the latest information and user preferences. This includes retrieving current settings, applying changes through updates, and removing outdated entries. The system provides functionality for both batch updates and individual setting management to streamline the administration process.',NULL),(91,22,53,'As a category administrator, I want to manage categories by creating, updating, retrieving, and deleting them so that I can maintain an organized and efficient categorization system. The system provides functionalities such as getting a list of categories, saving new categories, updating existing ones, and deleting categories by their ID. This allows me to ensure that the category data is accurate and up-to-date, supporting effective management of the content within the application.',NULL),(92,23,54,'As a website administrator, I want to log and manage visitor information, including UUIDs and IP addresses, so that I can track user behavior and ensure proper identification for security purposes. The system provides functionality to create visit logs, check UUID existence, and handle logging through various methods in the VisitLogAspect class. This allows me to monitor visits effectively while maintaining records of user interactions with the site.',NULL),(93,23,55,'As a visitor, I want to be able to save and delete my visit records and logs, so that I can manage my visit history effectively. The system provides functionality to save visitor information, log visits, and delete records as needed through services like VisitorService and VisitLogService. Additionally, the ability to synchronize visit information with the database ensures that all data is up-to-date and accessible whenever required.',NULL),(94,23,56,'As an admin user, I want to view visit logs by providing a unique identifier (UUID), date, and pagination parameters (page number and size) so that I can efficiently analyze user behavior over time. Additionally, I want the system to judge the behavior of visits based on specific criteria from request parameters and results so that I can assess patterns in user interactions and make informed decisions regarding user engagement.',NULL),(95,23,57,'As a website administrator, I want to retrieve visitor data by date and analyze new visitor sources from yesterday, so that I can understand traffic trends and improve user engagement. Additionally, I want to update the page views and last visit time for specific users using their UUIDs, ensuring accurate tracking of user interactions. This will help me monitor site performance and enhance the overall user experience.',NULL),(96,24,58,'As a user of the Friend Service, I want to manage my friends by adding, updating, and deleting friends, as well as viewing their information and published status, so that I can maintain an accurate and up-to-date friend list. This includes actions like retrieving the friend list, saving new friends, updating their published status or information content, and deleting friends when necessary. These functionalities ensure that I can effectively manage my social connections.',NULL),(97,25,59,'As a content creator, I want to manage tags associated with my blog posts by adding, updating, deleting, and retrieving tags based on various criteria (such as tag ID or name), so that I can effectively organize and categorize my content. This includes the ability to view all tags, save new tags, update existing ones, and delete tags when necessary. The system provides these functionalities through methods like getTagList, saveTag, updateTag, and deleteTagById.',NULL),(98,26,60,'As a user, I want to manage moments by viewing, adding likes, updating publication status, and deleting moments so that I can effectively curate and interact with content. The system allows me to retrieve a list of moments, view details of specific moments, add likes to enhance engagement, update their published status for visibility control, and delete moments when necessary. These actions collectively empower me to maintain an organized and relevant collection of moments.',NULL),(99,27,61,'As a user, I want to access and manage information about the application through features such as retrieving general information (getAboutInfo), updating details (updateAbout), and checking comment settings (getAboutCommentEnabled) so that I can ensure the content is accurate and relevant. Additionally, I want to be able to delete outdated cache data (deleteAboutRedisCache) to maintain system performance, ensuring that all interactions with the application are efficient and up-to-date.',NULL),(100,28,62,'As an admin user, I want to view and manage visitor statistics and blog metrics, so that I can analyze engagement and improve content strategies. This includes counting today\'s visit logs, retrieving blog and comment counts, accessing category and tag blog counts, and obtaining city visitor lists. By having these insights readily available through the dashboard interface, I can make informed decisions to enhance user experience and drive traffic effectively.',NULL),(101,29,63,'As a user of the system, I want to receive a structured result set that includes the total number of pages and a list of items, so that I can easily navigate through paginated data and access the information I need efficiently. The PageResult constructor allows for the initialization of these parameters, ensuring that users have clear visibility into how many pages are available and what content is present on each page, thereby enhancing my overall experience with the application.',NULL),(102,30,64,'As a user of the application, I want to receive clear error messages when my requests fail due to not found resources or persistence issues, so that I can understand what went wrong and take appropriate action. The system provides specific exception handlers for different scenarios, such as NotFoundException and PersistenceException, which capture the context of the error and return meaningful feedback. This ensures that users are informed about issues like missing data or database errors in a user-friendly manner.',NULL),(103,31,65,'As a user, I want to receive feedback on my actions through success and error messages so that I can understand the outcome of my requests. The system provides this feedback using methods like Result.ok() for successful operations and Result.error() for failures. Additionally, I want to access various content sections such as about, archives, categories, and tags through dedicated controller methods, allowing me to navigate the application effectively.',NULL),(104,32,66,'As a blog reader, I want to retrieve blog information by a specific hash and pagination number, so that I can easily access the content I am interested in without being overwhelmed by too much information at once. The methods \'getBlogInfoPageResultByHash\' in both \'RedisService\' and \'RedisServiceImpl\' provide this functionality, ensuring that I can obtain relevant blog data efficiently based on my specified criteria.',NULL),(105,32,67,'As a developer, I want to save various data structures (key-value pairs, maps, lists, and objects) into Redis storage so that I can efficiently manage and retrieve application data. The system provides methods to save key-value pairs to hashes, maps to hashes, lists to values, maps to values, objects to values, and values to sets. This functionality allows for flexible data organization and quick access in the application.',NULL),(106,32,68,'As a developer, I want to retrieve data from Redis using various methods such as getting maps by hash, values by hash key, and lists or objects by value so that I can efficiently access and manipulate data stored in the Redis database. The system provides functionality to get maps, values, lists, and objects based on specific keys or hashes, enabling streamlined data retrieval processes that support application performance and user experience.',NULL),(107,32,69,'As a developer, I want to increment values in a Redis database using both hash keys and regular keys, so that I can efficiently update counters or metrics without having to manually retrieve and modify the data. The system provides two key functionalities: \'incrementByHashKey\' allows for incrementing values associated with specific hash keys, while \'incrementByKey\' enables direct increments on standard keys. This ensures flexibility in managing data stored in Redis.',NULL),(108,32,70,'As a system administrator, I want to delete specific entries from the Redis cache by hash key, set value, or direct key, so that I can efficiently manage and maintain the integrity of cached data. The functions deleteByHashKey, deleteValueBySet, and deleteCacheByKey allow me to perform these actions across different implementations of RedisService. This ensures that outdated or unnecessary data is removed promptly, optimizing system performance and resource utilization.',NULL),(109,32,71,'As a user of the Redis service, I want to count the number of elements in a specific set using the countBySet function, so that I can quickly retrieve and analyze the size of data collections associated with a given key. This functionality is crucial for managing data efficiently, allowing me to understand usage patterns and make informed decisions based on the size of these sets.',NULL),(110,32,72,'As a user of the Redis service, I want to check if a specific value exists in a set associated with a given key, so that I can verify the presence of data efficiently. This functionality is provided by the methods \'hasValueInSet\' in both \'top.naccl.service.RedisService\' and \'top.naccl.service.impl.RedisServiceImpl\', allowing me to perform this action seamlessly within the system. By utilizing these methods, I can ensure data integrity and make informed decisions based on the existence of values.',NULL),(111,32,73,'As a user of the Redis service, I want to check if a specific key exists in the Redis database using the hasKey function, so that I can confirm the presence of data before performing further operations. This functionality is crucial for ensuring data integrity and optimizing system performance by preventing unnecessary actions on non-existent keys. The implementation in both top.naccl.service.RedisService and top.naccl.service.impl.RedisServiceImpl provides a reliable way to verify key existence.',NULL),(112,32,74,'As a system administrator, I want to set expiration times for keys in the Redis database using the expire function, so that I can manage data retention effectively and ensure that outdated information is automatically removed. The code provides a mechanism to specify a key and a duration, allowing me to control how long specific data remains accessible in the system. This functionality supports efficient resource management and maintains optimal performance by preventing unnecessary data accumulation.',NULL),(113,33,75,'As an admin user, I want to manage visitor information by viewing a list of visitors, deleting specific visitor records, and updating the about section of the application, so that I can maintain accurate and relevant content for users. Additionally, I want to access account details using a user profile and JWT token to ensure secure management of user accounts. This functionality collectively supports effective administration and enhances user engagement.',NULL);
